{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9f39b4b564345c38","name":"card_unit_raf_mitchell","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/WinterWar/units/card_unit_raf_mitchell","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"RAF MITCHELL","text":"Has Salvage while Guarded.","flavorText":"The North American B-25 Mitchell was an American medium bomber which was introduced in 1941 and used by many Allied air forces and in every theater of WWII. The Royal Air Force (RAF) acquired the B-25 Mitchell bombers through the Lend-Lease program, for a total of 700 aircraft delivered before the end of the war. The initial batch was designated Mitchell I and arrived in August 1941, and later the B-25 Cs and Ds were designated Mitchell II. By the end of 1942, the RAF had received 93 Mitchells (Marks I and II), with some deployed to No. 2 Group RAF. After the European invasion, RAF Mitchell squadrons moved to bases in France and Belgium in support of the Allied ground forces. Additionally, the Polish No. 305 Squadron which fought alongside RAF operated Mitchell IIs before transitioning to the de Havilland Mosquito, and various second-line RAF units used B-25s for reconnaissance missions.","faction":"Britain","type":"bomber","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":6,"operationCost":3,"attack":6,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_raf_mitchell","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_raf_mitchell_title","SourceString":"RAF MITCHELL","LocalizedString":"RAF MITCHELL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":6,"defense":4,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_raf_mitchell_text","SourceString":"Has Salvage while Guarded.","LocalizedString":"Has Salvage while Guarded."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_raf_mitchell_history","SourceString":"The North American B-25 Mitchell was an American medium bomber which was introduced in 1941 and used by many Allied air forces and in every theater of WWII. The Royal Air Force (RAF) acquired the B-25 Mitchell bombers through the Lend-Lease program, for a total of 700 aircraft delivered before the end of the war. The initial batch was designated Mitchell I and arrived in August 1941, and later the B-25 Cs and Ds were designated Mitchell II. By the end of 1942, the RAF had received 93 Mitchells (Marks I and II), with some deployed to No. 2 Group RAF. After the European invasion, RAF Mitchell squadrons moved to bases in France and Belgium in support of the Allied ground forces. Additionally, the Polish No. 305 Squadron which fought alongside RAF operated Mitchell IIs before transitioning to the de Havilland Mosquito, and various second-line RAF units used B-25s for reconnaissance missions.","LocalizedString":"The North American B-25 Mitchell was an American medium bomber which was introduced in 1941 and used by many Allied air forces and in every theater of WWII. The Royal Air Force (RAF) acquired the B-25 Mitchell bombers through the Lend-Lease program, for a total of 700 aircraft delivered before the end of the war. The initial batch was designated Mitchell I and arrived in August 1941, and later the B-25 Cs and Ds were designated Mitchell II. By the end of 1942, the RAF had received 93 Mitchells (Marks I and II), with some deployed to No. 2 Group RAF. After the European invasion, RAF Mitchell squadrons moved to bases in France and Belgium in support of the Allied ground forces. Additionally, the Polish No. 305 Squadron which fought alongside RAF operated Mitchell IIs before transitioning to the de Havilland Mosquito, and various second-line RAF units used B-25s for reconnaissance missions."},"operationCost":3,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardAblitiesChanged","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardLocationMoved"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBub